; a vertical structural surface. barrier to horizontal motion.
; walls define rooms, buildings, enclosures.
; collision with wall: normal force is horizontal (perpendicular to wall surface).
; a ball thrown at a wall: horizontal velocity component reverses (times e).
; vertical component is unaffected by the wall collision.
; 
; wall as constraint: the ball cannot pass through.
; wall exerts normal force in the direction away from the wall.
; in 3d: static rigid body with vertical orientation.
; material of wall determines coefficient of restitution:
; concrete wall: e ≈ 0.5-0.6. padded wall: e ≈ 0.2. elastic wall: e ≈ 0.9.

(kosha wall
  (vishesa structures-varga common-sense-varga)
  (swarupa vertical barrier)
  (yukta normal-force collision-varga domain-3d))
